<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean stock watchdog finds unfair trading.</title>
<headline>S.Korean stock watchdog finds unfair trading.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Supervisory Board said on Friday it had uncovered unfair stock trading by 13 people involving the shares of four companies.</p>
<p>They were found to have been involved in manipulating share prices or failing to report to the authorities on their ownership status, the board said.</p>
<p>The four firms named by the board are Enkay Wire and Cable, Hangdo Merchant Bank, Shin Kwang Dyeing Industrial and Hansung Enterprise.</p>
<p>The board said 12 of the 13 people had been reported to prosecutors and the other to his company.</p>
<p>-- Seoul newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
